1
00:01:26,267 --> 00:01:27,884
I'm heading out.

2
00:01:28,352 --> 00:01:29,786
Okay.

3
00:01:31,555 --> 00:01:33,623
Feed Oscar, please.

4
00:01:40,030 --> 00:01:41,999
Have fun while I'm gone.

5
00:01:46,303 --> 00:01:48,405
Why does Oscar look so weak?

6
00:01:49,940 --> 00:01:51,541
Is he hungry?

7
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:08,925
Why didn't you...

8
00:02:12,338 --> 00:02:14,831
feed Oscar...

9
00:02:24,534 --> 00:02:26,510
I don't like that woman.

10
00:02:34,467 --> 00:02:36,086
Dad,

11
00:02:39,742 --> 00:02:42,392
can't you break up with her?

12
00:02:50,392 --> 00:02:52,169
Then should I...

13
00:02:56,601 --> 00:02:58,975
go back to Mom?

14
00:03:09,853 --> 00:03:15,059
I used to feel tired but proud after work,

15
00:03:15,059 --> 00:03:17,394
but now I'm walking on eggshells
around the director,

16
00:03:17,394 --> 00:03:19,396
and it feels uncomfortable.

17
00:03:19,396 --> 00:03:22,100
Right? We have way fewer expecting mothers.

18
00:03:22,100 --> 00:03:24,540
I like that it's quiet lately.

19
00:03:24,540 --> 00:03:27,037
Hey, being quiet means

20
00:03:27,037 --> 00:03:30,040
they don't need this many staff.

21
00:03:30,040 --> 00:03:31,741
Especially us.

22
00:03:32,250 --> 00:03:36,113
We're feeling down and have energy to spare,

23
00:03:36,113 --> 00:03:37,615
so should we go out for a team dinner?

24
00:03:37,615 --> 00:03:38,682
- Sounds good.
- Let's do it.

25
00:03:38,682 --> 00:03:39,850
I'm in.

26
00:03:39,850 --> 00:03:41,819
- Where to?
- I want tripe.

27
00:03:41,819 --> 00:03:43,567
I want lamb skewers.

28
00:03:43,567 --> 00:03:44,934
- How many rounds?
- Yes, Do Hyun.

29
00:03:44,934 --> 00:03:46,234
- We have to go at least three rounds.
- Of course.

30
00:03:46,234 --> 00:03:48,400
- First round, lamb skewers.
- Tripe, lamb skewers.

31
00:03:48,400 --> 00:03:50,594
Uh, I just finished work...

32
00:03:52,129 --> 00:03:54,631
Do Hyun, are you drunk? At this hour?

33
00:03:55,501 --> 00:03:57,100
We're going to have a blast.

34
00:04:23,980 --> 00:04:25,529
Do Hyun.

35
00:04:41,512 --> 00:04:43,180
Are you okay?

36
00:04:49,153 --> 00:04:50,654
I'm sorry.

37
00:04:54,458 --> 00:04:56,693
Do you want to walk a bit?

38
00:05:08,539 --> 00:05:10,240
Daniel kept saying he was okay.

39
00:05:12,442 --> 00:05:14,110
He just kept insisting

40
00:05:16,284 --> 00:05:18,481
he was fine,

41
00:05:19,934 --> 00:05:21,318
so I...

42
00:05:22,200 --> 00:05:24,815
Obviously, there's no way

43
00:05:24,815 --> 00:05:26,523
he could be okay.

44
00:05:29,968 --> 00:05:31,728
But I honestly didn't know.

45
00:05:36,535 --> 00:05:38,568
Of course you didn't know.

46
00:05:40,295 --> 00:05:42,405
No one ever knows.

47
00:05:43,795 --> 00:05:46,876
They hide it desperately

48
00:05:47,578 --> 00:05:50,780
without saying a word.

49
00:05:58,520 --> 00:06:00,234
I...

50
00:06:00,234 --> 00:06:02,859
I want to get along with Daniel.

51
00:06:09,934 --> 00:06:11,468
Why?

52
00:06:11,468 --> 00:06:13,194
Do you think it won't work?

53
00:06:13,194 --> 00:06:14,638
No...

54
00:06:15,439 --> 00:06:17,007
I...

55
00:06:18,375 --> 00:06:21,011
just don't know what to do...

56
00:06:24,915 --> 00:06:26,683
I'll do it.

57
00:06:29,395 --> 00:06:33,323
Daniel has his own way and pace,

58
00:06:34,391 --> 00:06:37,827
so I don't know when or what it'll be,

59
00:06:39,909 --> 00:06:43,133
but I'll keep looking for an opportunity.

60
00:06:44,701 --> 00:06:47,203
Who knows? It might be sooner than we think.

61
00:07:01,585 --> 00:07:03,553
I really...

62
00:07:04,855 --> 00:07:06,901
didn't expect you...

63
00:07:06,901 --> 00:07:09,192
to say that.

64
00:07:11,850 --> 00:07:14,031
Daniel's feelings...

65
00:07:14,031 --> 00:07:15,501
I can't...

66
00:07:15,501 --> 00:07:17,801
do anything about them,

67
00:07:18,969 --> 00:07:21,371
and it'll be hard on you, too.

68
00:07:24,408 --> 00:07:26,843
I keep worrying... what if you leave me?

69
00:07:27,950 --> 00:07:30,747
What if you abandon me?

70
00:07:33,767 --> 00:07:37,400
You really are an artist.

71
00:07:37,400 --> 00:07:40,023
No joke.

72
00:07:46,563 --> 00:07:48,598
[Catholic Church]

73
00:07:48,598 --> 00:07:51,567
Two single adults

74
00:07:51,567 --> 00:07:54,037
spent the night together.

75
00:07:54,037 --> 00:07:56,172
With mutual consent.

76
00:07:57,734 --> 00:07:59,843
What's the problem?

77
00:08:01,104 --> 00:08:02,912
It's not

78
00:08:04,133 --> 00:08:06,049
a problem, strictly speaking...

79
00:08:06,049 --> 00:08:07,951
Was it a one-time fling?

80
00:08:07,951 --> 00:08:10,067
Oh, no!

81
00:08:10,067 --> 00:08:13,590
- It wasn't really a fling...
- Then it must be love.

82
00:08:14,658 --> 00:08:16,234
Well...

83
00:08:16,234 --> 00:08:18,501
it's not exactly love, either...

84
00:08:18,501 --> 00:08:20,230
Well...

85
00:08:20,931 --> 00:08:24,568
What is troubling you

86
00:08:24,568 --> 00:08:26,136
the most right now?

87
00:08:26,838 --> 00:08:31,108
We first met in kindergarten.

88
00:08:31,108 --> 00:08:32,642
And?

89
00:08:33,325 --> 00:08:35,300
I mean...

90
00:08:35,300 --> 00:08:36,780
If things go south,

91
00:08:36,780 --> 00:08:38,815
I'm afraid it'll ruin

92
00:08:38,815 --> 00:08:40,450
our 20-year friendship.

93
00:08:40,450 --> 00:08:42,552
So what if it does?

94
00:08:44,044 --> 00:08:45,745
Excuse me?

95
00:08:45,745 --> 00:08:49,759
I asked, so what if a 20-year friendship ends?

96
00:08:51,701 --> 00:08:53,263
Well...

97
00:08:57,367 --> 00:08:59,836
[For the Faithful]

98
00:08:59,836 --> 00:09:01,738
Occupied.

99
00:09:04,915 --> 00:09:06,275
Hey,

100
00:09:06,275 --> 00:09:08,012
get out of here.

101
00:09:08,012 --> 00:09:09,279
Huh?

102
00:09:10,214 --> 00:09:12,315
I said, get out.

103
00:09:19,957 --> 00:09:23,026
Aren't you too old
to be getting beaten up like this?

104
00:09:23,761 --> 00:09:26,215
I didn't get beaten up, Father.

105
00:09:26,215 --> 00:09:28,331
It was an act of punishment and revenge.

106
00:09:28,331 --> 00:09:30,200
Jeez...

107
00:09:30,200 --> 00:09:33,904
Like father, like son. You're just like him.

108
00:09:33,904 --> 00:09:35,205
What?

109
00:09:36,404 --> 00:09:39,509
Just call me Hyung, like the old days.

110
00:09:41,801 --> 00:09:43,580
Okay... Hyung.

111
00:09:44,681 --> 00:09:46,834
So...

112
00:09:46,834 --> 00:09:49,724
It's between love and friendship. Right?

113
00:09:49,724 --> 00:09:51,821
That same old cliche.

114
00:09:52,567 --> 00:09:56,159
You can't really sum us up that simply, but...

115
00:09:56,960 --> 00:09:59,000
You know about Jun Kyung and me

116
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:01,231
back in our school days, right?

117
00:10:02,984 --> 00:10:06,002
Can you call that a relationship?

118
00:10:06,914 --> 00:10:08,868
If anything,

119
00:10:08,868 --> 00:10:10,240
she wasn't into you.

120
00:10:10,240 --> 00:10:13,443
You chased her around spreading rumors,

121
00:10:13,443 --> 00:10:15,278
then my mom threw water on you.

122
00:10:15,278 --> 00:10:17,481
Back in my prime, full of energy...

123
00:10:17,481 --> 00:10:21,184
why did I give up on Jun Kyung
instead of enduring that humiliation?

124
00:10:21,834 --> 00:10:23,225
What?

125
00:10:25,555 --> 00:10:28,224
I chose friendship back then.

126
00:10:28,758 --> 00:10:31,794
I was torn between love and friendship.

127
00:10:33,728 --> 00:10:36,633
For the sake of some great friendship...

128
00:10:38,434 --> 00:10:40,070
Hey.

129
00:10:40,070 --> 00:10:43,606
- You were never her type.
- Shut up.

130
00:10:45,499 --> 00:10:48,011
Friendship, my foot.

131
00:10:48,011 --> 00:10:50,847
You just lacked the courage and confidence.

132
00:10:51,680 --> 00:10:55,718
It's nothing more than a loser's excuse.

133
00:10:58,021 --> 00:11:00,123
Do you honestly not like her?

134
00:11:04,057 --> 00:11:06,596
Why worry if you don't like her?

135
00:11:38,628 --> 00:11:40,697
He looks perfectly fine.

136
00:11:42,332 --> 00:11:44,601
What a complete moron.

137
00:11:45,269 --> 00:11:46,730
Listen up!

138
00:11:47,804 --> 00:11:49,841
It's sudden, but...

139
00:11:49,841 --> 00:11:51,875
Our marketer, Hwang Beom Jun,

140
00:11:51,875 --> 00:11:55,645
just handed in his resignation.

141
00:11:55,645 --> 00:11:57,981
He feels bad, so he's treating us tonight.

142
00:11:57,981 --> 00:12:00,499
Let's all go out after work.

143
00:12:00,499 --> 00:12:03,220
Let's make him spend big before he goes.

144
00:12:03,220 --> 00:12:05,488
He said he's buying something expensive!

145
00:12:05,488 --> 00:12:08,057
See you later! I'll treat you to a great meal!

146
00:12:11,928 --> 00:12:13,564
That is so cool...

147
00:12:13,564 --> 00:12:17,734
Quitting for love...
and leaving for Europe indefinitely.

148
00:12:19,002 --> 00:12:22,389
I wish I were your age, Beom Jun.

149
00:12:22,389 --> 00:12:24,501
It's not too late

150
00:12:24,501 --> 00:12:26,609
for you yet, Chief.

151
00:12:27,143 --> 00:12:28,878
I don't have the courage. Or the talent.

152
00:12:28,878 --> 00:12:29,949
Talent wouldn't be enough, anyway.

153
00:12:29,949 --> 00:12:32,482
Only people who work for fun can do that.

154
00:12:32,482 --> 00:12:35,185
So, where in Europe are you going?

155
00:12:35,185 --> 00:12:39,288
She said she wants to visit Estonia,

156
00:12:39,852 --> 00:12:42,692
so we'll start with the Baltic states.

157
00:12:43,727 --> 00:12:44,813
The Baltic states...

158
00:12:44,813 --> 00:12:47,131
I've only heard of them in books.

159
00:12:47,131 --> 00:12:49,065
Where are the Baltic states?

160
00:12:51,701 --> 00:12:53,270
- Is she leaving?
- Is she heading out?

161
00:12:53,270 --> 00:12:54,671
I guess so.

162
00:13:12,868 --> 00:13:15,325
I'm telling you, that's not it.

163
00:13:15,325 --> 00:13:16,334
Drop it.

164
00:13:16,334 --> 00:13:18,728
- I'm sick of hearing that.
- Oh, cake!

165
00:13:18,728 --> 00:13:19,534
What?

166
00:13:19,534 --> 00:13:21,467
See? That's the spirit.

167
00:13:21,467 --> 00:13:23,434
It is a farewell party, after all.

168
00:13:23,434 --> 00:13:25,601
- Really?
- Did she slip out to get that cake?

169
00:13:27,837 --> 00:13:29,418
Congratulations.

170
00:13:29,418 --> 00:13:32,758
Have a great trip to Europe
with your girlfriend.

171
00:13:32,758 --> 00:13:35,111
Thank you...

172
00:13:42,686 --> 00:13:44,153
Right...

173
00:13:45,388 --> 00:13:48,958
You're just being true to your feelings.
I'm the idiot.

174
00:13:49,526 --> 00:13:51,094
What the...

175
00:13:51,767 --> 00:13:53,923
- What?
- What?

176
00:13:54,467 --> 00:13:55,667
- What was...
- What's going on?

177
00:13:55,667 --> 00:13:57,967
Why did she do that?

178
00:13:58,734 --> 00:14:01,467
So for Ms. Oh Mi Ja's 80th birthday...

179
00:14:01,467 --> 00:14:03,073
Got it.

180
00:14:03,073 --> 00:14:05,575
I'm not that stingy.

181
00:14:05,575 --> 00:14:08,177
If you order over 300 towels,
I'll just throw everything in for you.

182
00:14:13,383 --> 00:14:15,853
Quiet down, I'm on the phone.

183
00:14:15,853 --> 00:14:18,154
No, no! Yes, go ahead.

184
00:14:18,154 --> 00:14:19,289
Right.

185
00:14:19,289 --> 00:14:23,459
We'll do that for you. Okay, thank you.

186
00:14:24,995 --> 00:14:26,429
- Jin Ho.
- What?

187
00:14:26,429 --> 00:14:28,431
What brings you here without calling?

188
00:14:30,100 --> 00:14:31,601
Hey.

189
00:14:37,454 --> 00:14:38,239
Hello.

190
00:14:38,239 --> 00:14:40,795
You got my text, right?

191
00:14:40,795 --> 00:14:42,036
Yes.

192
00:14:42,036 --> 00:14:44,347
100 each of gray, pink, and white...

193
00:14:44,347 --> 00:14:46,683
Yes. Please have them ready by the 15th.

194
00:14:46,683 --> 00:14:48,619
Thank you.

195
00:14:48,619 --> 00:14:50,815
Please understand.

196
00:14:50,815 --> 00:14:52,790
You know how she is.

197
00:14:52,790 --> 00:14:54,334
What's wrong with her?

198
00:14:54,334 --> 00:14:56,058
She's the best.

199
00:14:57,327 --> 00:15:01,235
Did all the nice people die off?

200
00:15:01,235 --> 00:15:05,635
I'm not asking her to be soft like a new towel.

201
00:15:06,504 --> 00:15:08,099
But

202
00:15:08,099 --> 00:15:10,206
she shouldn't be scratchy

203
00:15:10,206 --> 00:15:12,542
like a scrub towel.

204
00:15:14,144 --> 00:15:15,913
What about a scrub towel?

205
00:15:15,913 --> 00:15:17,380
You scared me.

206
00:15:18,848 --> 00:15:20,383
When did you get here?

207
00:15:20,383 --> 00:15:21,217
What about the shop?

208
00:15:21,217 --> 00:15:23,619
It's empty. So you go. Hurry.

209
00:15:24,139 --> 00:15:25,474
What?

210
00:15:27,024 --> 00:15:28,724
Okay...

211
00:15:31,662 --> 00:15:34,197
I'll come visit you soon.

212
00:15:53,550 --> 00:15:58,454
When she first brought you home to get married,

213
00:16:00,089 --> 00:16:03,926
everyone was against it. It was chaos.

214
00:16:06,473 --> 00:16:09,074
- I'm sure they were.
- Right.

215
00:16:09,074 --> 00:16:11,534
I mean, considering your ages back then...

216
00:16:13,194 --> 00:16:15,834
But you know I was the only one

217
00:16:15,834 --> 00:16:17,208
who approved?

218
00:16:17,208 --> 00:16:18,774
Of course. I know.

219
00:16:43,257 --> 00:16:46,871
My sister asked me why I approved.

220
00:16:46,871 --> 00:16:48,971
What do you think I told her?

221
00:16:52,379 --> 00:16:56,079
I said you looked tacky,
so you wouldn't be popular with women.

222
00:16:56,079 --> 00:16:57,734
Meaning

223
00:16:57,734 --> 00:17:00,950
you would never cheat.

224
00:17:03,684 --> 00:17:06,137
I don't know what to say in this situation...

225
00:17:06,137 --> 00:17:08,157
But, really... It's a genuine

226
00:17:08,157 --> 00:17:09,225
- misunderstanding.
- No.

227
00:17:09,225 --> 00:17:12,396
You don't have the guts to cheat

228
00:17:12,396 --> 00:17:15,197
while my sister is still alive.

229
00:17:16,467 --> 00:17:19,534
Why wouldn't I know?

230
00:17:23,149 --> 00:17:25,834
My husband just laughs it off

231
00:17:25,834 --> 00:17:28,077
when people don't pay him.

232
00:17:28,077 --> 00:17:31,213
I've watched that for over 20 years.

233
00:17:32,801 --> 00:17:35,464
Maybe I'm just selfish...

234
00:17:35,464 --> 00:17:39,322
but seeing my husband makes my blood boil.

235
00:17:40,480 --> 00:17:42,325
If

236
00:17:43,334 --> 00:17:47,063
he had an accident and ended up like that...

237
00:17:48,532 --> 00:17:52,368
and I had to change his diapers
for seven years...

238
00:17:53,534 --> 00:17:56,239
and put up with that temper...

239
00:17:56,239 --> 00:18:00,100
there is no way

240
00:18:00,100 --> 00:18:02,511
I could've done that.

241
00:18:04,818 --> 00:18:07,750
But he probably would.

242
00:18:08,760 --> 00:18:10,553
Because he's a fool.

243
00:18:14,652 --> 00:18:17,660
Even if we're family...

244
00:18:17,660 --> 00:18:20,529
I only thought about my poor sister.

245
00:18:21,197 --> 00:18:23,432
I never thought

246
00:18:25,400 --> 00:18:26,403
about how hard it was for you.

247
00:18:26,403 --> 00:18:28,571
I'm sorry.

248
00:18:29,334 --> 00:18:31,107
No, don't be.

249
00:18:54,865 --> 00:18:58,134
I still can't congratulate you on that woman...

250
00:18:58,835 --> 00:19:03,606
I won't until the day I die...

251
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:09,445
But thank you

252
00:19:10,601 --> 00:19:12,648
for taking care of my sister.

253
00:19:15,519 --> 00:19:18,054
Thank you so much.

254
00:19:35,405 --> 00:19:38,868
- Get home safe.
- Bye.

255
00:19:38,868 --> 00:19:41,043
Stop mumbling.

256
00:19:42,578 --> 00:19:45,349
- Is this fun?
- Yeah, it's fun!

257
00:19:45,349 --> 00:19:47,316
Let's go for round two!

258
00:20:05,926 --> 00:20:08,404
Why are you always sitting over there?

259
00:20:09,686 --> 00:20:12,074
Is this the only place you have to go?

260
00:20:13,110 --> 00:20:15,144
Do you think my house is a joke?

261
00:20:17,257 --> 00:20:18,881
Why are you

262
00:20:19,601 --> 00:20:21,352
being so prickly?

263
00:20:21,352 --> 00:20:23,052
Why are you here?

264
00:20:25,556 --> 00:20:26,687
What happened to your face?

265
00:20:26,687 --> 00:20:28,657
I asked why you're here.

266
00:20:34,343 --> 00:20:38,000
I thought I should apologize.

267
00:20:42,130 --> 00:20:44,343
Apologize for what?

268
00:20:44,343 --> 00:20:45,875
I just

269
00:20:46,834 --> 00:20:49,778
broke up with Sol recently...

270
00:20:52,216 --> 00:20:54,150
- And...
- Forget it.

271
00:20:55,923 --> 00:20:58,387
My feelings are my own.

272
00:20:58,387 --> 00:21:00,589
I don't expect anything from you.

273
00:21:03,419 --> 00:21:05,661
So you don't need to say more.

274
00:21:07,998 --> 00:21:09,565
Okay...

275
00:21:10,768 --> 00:21:12,399
Actually,

276
00:21:12,399 --> 00:21:14,103
there is one thing.

277
00:21:15,306 --> 00:21:16,772
What is it?

278
00:21:17,287 --> 00:21:19,875
- Anything I can do...
- Tell them

279
00:21:21,601 --> 00:21:23,612
you'll do the internship again.

280
00:21:24,827 --> 00:21:26,674
- What?
- You said you regretted

281
00:21:26,674 --> 00:21:29,051
doing nothing before your mom passed away.

282
00:21:30,753 --> 00:21:33,489
And you know I played a part in that, right?

283
00:21:34,657 --> 00:21:37,000
So get it back

284
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:39,028
and buy me a proper meal.

285
00:21:50,007 --> 00:21:51,507
And

286
00:21:53,968 --> 00:21:56,612
stop walking on eggshells!

287
00:21:57,413 --> 00:22:00,983
Some people quit their jobs and act so proud.

288
00:22:00,983 --> 00:22:04,453
They break up on a whim
and go to Europe together.

289
00:22:05,047 --> 00:22:06,922
But look at us...

290
00:22:08,434 --> 00:22:10,960
Why are we such idiots?

291
00:22:11,501 --> 00:22:13,028
Ugh!

292
00:22:55,283 --> 00:22:57,473
You have no idea how happy I am.

293
00:23:00,511 --> 00:23:02,044
That you came

294
00:23:04,033 --> 00:23:06,181
to see me like this.

295
00:23:39,100 --> 00:23:40,749
Daniel.

296
00:23:49,093 --> 00:23:51,771
I came because I have something to say.

297
00:24:02,534 --> 00:24:03,945
What?

298
00:24:08,244 --> 00:24:09,245
Hey, kid!

299
00:24:09,245 --> 00:24:12,114
Watch where you're going.

300
00:24:12,114 --> 00:24:15,584
What are you doing? He fell and got hurt.

301
00:24:17,043 --> 00:24:18,527
I didn't hit him.

302
00:24:18,527 --> 00:24:21,423
He fell on his own.

303
00:24:21,423 --> 00:24:23,403
He's just a kid! Like you said.

304
00:24:23,403 --> 00:24:26,696
You should've asked if he was okay first.

305
00:24:26,696 --> 00:24:29,066
Cars drive through here...

306
00:24:29,066 --> 00:24:31,063
He shouldn't be riding that...

307
00:24:31,063 --> 00:24:32,335
Who are you, anyway?

308
00:24:32,335 --> 00:24:35,104
Are you his mom?

309
00:24:35,104 --> 00:24:36,344
Yes.

310
00:24:38,422 --> 00:24:40,075
I am his mom.

311
00:24:46,048 --> 00:24:47,683
Let me see.

312
00:25:01,998 --> 00:25:03,365
I'm sorry.

313
00:25:06,635 --> 00:25:09,705
For saying you're my mom earlier?

314
00:25:11,976 --> 00:25:13,375
No.

315
00:25:17,646 --> 00:25:19,915
For not asking if you were okay first,

316
00:25:20,901 --> 00:25:24,853
or if you were hurt.

317
00:25:26,634 --> 00:25:29,458
Even though I had plenty of chances.

318
00:25:40,000 --> 00:25:41,770
I asked Dad

319
00:25:43,667 --> 00:25:46,575
to break up with you.

320
00:25:48,577 --> 00:25:50,045
I...

321
00:25:50,968 --> 00:25:52,414
regretted it.

322
00:25:54,351 --> 00:25:55,818
Why?

323
00:25:57,704 --> 00:25:59,888
I don't like you,

324
00:26:01,968 --> 00:26:04,993
but I don't want Dad to be sad, either.

325
00:26:09,160 --> 00:26:11,300
You don't like me either, right?

326
00:26:15,805 --> 00:26:18,774
Who likes someone who hates them?

327
00:26:23,345 --> 00:26:24,980
Ouch!

328
00:26:28,050 --> 00:26:30,252
Wear protective gear from now on.

329
00:26:31,789 --> 00:26:33,624
But

330
00:26:33,624 --> 00:26:35,324
that doesn't look cool.

331
00:26:42,455 --> 00:26:44,166
I'm hungry.

332
00:26:46,504 --> 00:26:48,270
Do you want to go eat?

333
00:27:05,656 --> 00:27:07,189
Isn't it spicy?

334
00:27:08,726 --> 00:27:10,459
I'm practicing.

335
00:27:12,762 --> 00:27:15,998
If it's spicy, just don't eat it. Why practice?

336
00:27:17,982 --> 00:27:19,968
Because I want to get along...

337
00:27:20,638 --> 00:27:22,271
with people.

338
00:27:38,787 --> 00:27:40,722
Can I ask you something?

339
00:27:45,331 --> 00:27:47,701
Why Oscar?

340
00:27:47,701 --> 00:27:49,264
The fish's name.

341
00:27:54,003 --> 00:27:55,704
Do I...

342
00:27:57,200 --> 00:27:58,740
have to say?

343
00:28:04,594 --> 00:28:06,615
It's the name

344
00:28:08,767 --> 00:28:11,300
of a kid

345
00:28:11,300 --> 00:28:13,288
who bullied me in Germany.

346
00:28:15,159 --> 00:28:17,326
The kid I hated the most.

347
00:28:20,898 --> 00:28:22,833
Ah...

348
00:28:22,833 --> 00:28:24,333
I see.

349
00:28:26,538 --> 00:28:28,070
I'm sorry.

350
00:28:28,785 --> 00:28:30,672
I'll change the name.

351
00:28:33,364 --> 00:28:34,977
No.

352
00:28:36,858 --> 00:28:39,047
I like that name.

353
00:28:49,293 --> 00:28:50,892
Is it better now?

354
00:28:54,096 --> 00:28:55,664
Did the milk help?

355
00:28:55,664 --> 00:28:57,775
It's my first time, but it's pretty good.

356
00:28:57,775 --> 00:28:59,535
First time?

357
00:28:59,535 --> 00:29:01,823
He never bought it for you?

358
00:29:16,400 --> 00:29:18,520
It's good. Eat up.

359
00:29:27,667 --> 00:29:29,665
It's so good.

360
00:29:29,665 --> 00:29:30,766
What is this?

361
00:29:30,766 --> 00:29:32,835
You're only serving the Guide.

362
00:29:32,835 --> 00:29:35,539
That's the tyranny
of the one holding the tongs.

363
00:29:35,539 --> 00:29:37,827
Oh, it's not tyranny...

364
00:29:37,827 --> 00:29:39,167
So don't just give me some.

365
00:29:39,167 --> 00:29:40,711
You should eat, too, Jin Ho.

366
00:29:40,711 --> 00:29:41,887
What?

367
00:29:41,887 --> 00:29:44,288
- Eat up.
- What's going on with you two?

368
00:29:44,288 --> 00:29:46,148
What is it?

369
00:29:46,148 --> 00:29:50,168
The way you look at each other is suspicious.

370
00:29:50,168 --> 00:29:51,053
Wait...

371
00:29:51,053 --> 00:29:54,801
Are you dating the Guide or something?

372
00:29:54,801 --> 00:29:55,591
Excuse me?

373
00:29:55,591 --> 00:29:57,826
He's not denying it.

374
00:29:57,826 --> 00:29:59,528
No way!

375
00:29:59,528 --> 00:30:01,530
What?

376
00:30:02,066 --> 00:30:03,598
For real?

377
00:30:04,400 --> 00:30:06,468
- What?
- What?

378
00:30:06,468 --> 00:30:09,071
Yes. We're dating.

379
00:30:31,994 --> 00:30:34,029
Why don't you sing a song?

380
00:30:34,029 --> 00:30:36,732
I'm a terrible singer. You sing another one.

381
00:30:36,732 --> 00:30:38,651
Do you think you're at a concert?

382
00:30:38,651 --> 00:30:41,422
Pay the entrance fee or start singing.
Pick one!

383
00:30:42,706 --> 00:30:43,372
- I'm not good...
- Pick one.

384
00:30:43,372 --> 00:30:44,808
Just sing one song.

385
00:30:44,808 --> 00:30:46,908
I'll do it. I'll sing.

386
00:31:14,536 --> 00:31:16,205
You look really happy today.

387
00:31:16,205 --> 00:31:17,975
Yes. I am.

388
00:31:17,975 --> 00:31:19,154
Right.

389
00:31:19,154 --> 00:31:21,410
We only took that one trip together,

390
00:31:21,410 --> 00:31:22,803
but here we are,
the whole group still meeting up,

391
00:31:22,803 --> 00:31:24,546
laughing, and supporting each other.

392
00:31:24,546 --> 00:31:27,082
The reason I was truly happy today

393
00:31:27,082 --> 00:31:29,752
is that we didn't hide our relationship.

394
00:31:29,752 --> 00:31:32,114
We didn't have to care what others thought.

395
00:31:32,114 --> 00:31:33,507
Me too.

396
00:31:35,292 --> 00:31:36,992
Ja Yeong...

397
00:31:38,167 --> 00:31:40,061
I have a favor to ask.

398
00:31:40,923 --> 00:31:43,300
If you do me a favor first,

399
00:31:43,300 --> 00:31:45,800
I'll listen.

400
00:31:47,338 --> 00:31:49,073
Okay.

401
00:31:49,073 --> 00:31:50,839
Tell me. I'll do it.

402
00:31:51,909 --> 00:31:55,079
Sing a song for me.

403
00:31:55,079 --> 00:31:56,563
What?

404
00:31:56,563 --> 00:31:58,004
No way...

405
00:31:58,004 --> 00:31:59,084
I really can't sing.

406
00:31:59,084 --> 00:32:00,104
Then I can't grant your favor, either.

407
00:32:00,104 --> 00:32:02,152
Come on... That's not fair.

408
00:32:02,152 --> 00:32:04,152
How about I give you a piggyback ride instead?

409
00:32:04,622 --> 00:32:05,723
No.

410
00:32:05,723 --> 00:32:07,355
I'm really bad at it.

411
00:32:08,592 --> 00:32:10,192
Okay then, don't laugh.

412
00:32:11,033 --> 00:32:12,427
Now?

413
00:32:13,238 --> 00:32:14,996
Right here?

414
00:32:15,831 --> 00:32:17,966
Then where and when else should I do it?

415
00:32:19,635 --> 00:32:21,372
Don't laugh.

416
00:32:21,372 --> 00:32:23,040
Promise me.

417
00:32:23,040 --> 00:32:24,372
Promise.

418
00:32:25,738 --> 00:32:27,442
Just stay...

419
00:32:29,244 --> 00:32:30,879
Don't laugh.

420
00:32:33,779 --> 00:32:37,018
♪ Just stay ♪

421
00:32:38,000 --> 00:32:40,889
♪ by my side ♪

422
00:32:41,490 --> 00:32:43,792
♪ You must not ♪

423
00:32:44,434 --> 00:32:47,596
♪ leave ♪

424
00:32:52,601 --> 00:32:56,104
♪ Leaving longing ♪

425
00:32:56,801 --> 00:33:00,475
♪ behind on the long road ♪

426
00:33:01,594 --> 00:33:05,380
♪ You can't return ♪

427
00:33:05,380 --> 00:33:10,385
♪ in search of a rainbow ♪

428
00:34:15,334 --> 00:34:17,619
♪ In the cold wind ♪

429
00:34:18,167 --> 00:34:22,167
♪ that blows ♪

430
00:34:22,167 --> 00:34:27,495
♪ You cry alone ♪

431
00:34:29,831 --> 00:34:34,434
♪ But I'll always stay ♪

432
00:34:34,434 --> 00:34:38,306
♪ by your side ♪

433
00:34:39,601 --> 00:34:45,447
♪ I'll never leave you ♪

434
00:34:56,058 --> 00:34:58,028
I really can't sing, can I?

435
00:34:58,028 --> 00:34:59,404
No.

436
00:35:00,264 --> 00:35:01,896
It was wonderful.

437
00:35:04,068 --> 00:35:05,734
Really?

438
00:35:07,603 --> 00:35:09,004
Now,

439
00:35:09,004 --> 00:35:12,142
tell me your favor. I'll grant it.

440
00:35:13,434 --> 00:35:14,560
Well,

441
00:35:14,560 --> 00:35:16,344
Ja Yeong...

442
00:35:17,968 --> 00:35:19,547
You see...

443
00:35:21,917 --> 00:35:24,019
Dinner with your family?

444
00:35:25,454 --> 00:35:28,726
If it feels like too much, we can wait a while.

445
00:35:28,726 --> 00:35:31,326
Too much? Why would it be too much?

446
00:35:33,562 --> 00:35:34,963
Really?

447
00:35:36,131 --> 00:35:38,533
Then bring Daniel along.

448
00:35:38,533 --> 00:35:41,302
I told Dad and Jun Seo about Daniel.

449
00:35:42,620 --> 00:35:45,340
Ah! If Daniel says he wants to...

450
00:35:45,340 --> 00:35:47,175
let's all meet together.

451
00:36:06,128 --> 00:36:08,363
Thanks for driving me home.

452
00:36:09,431 --> 00:36:12,829
I'm the one who should be thankful today.

453
00:36:12,829 --> 00:36:15,737
You're just saying thanks?
Aren't you forgetting something?

454
00:36:28,316 --> 00:36:30,552
Dad?

455
00:36:32,534 --> 00:36:33,954
Yeah.

456
00:36:35,624 --> 00:36:37,000
It's a pleasure to meet you.

457
00:36:37,000 --> 00:36:38,693
Ah, yes.

458
00:36:42,397 --> 00:36:43,695
Dad.

459
00:36:43,695 --> 00:36:45,133
Yeah.

460
00:36:45,133 --> 00:36:47,869
You should have called before coming.

461
00:36:49,455 --> 00:36:51,934
I had a gathering nearby

462
00:36:51,934 --> 00:36:53,775
and just stopped by.

463
00:36:58,413 --> 00:37:00,337
That guy was handsome.

464
00:37:00,337 --> 00:37:02,050
- Ah...
- He made a good impression.

465
00:37:02,050 --> 00:37:04,185
Right.

466
00:37:12,294 --> 00:37:14,762
- Here are some tissues.
- Oh, thanks.

467
00:37:16,167 --> 00:37:17,766
I'll get it.

468
00:37:17,766 --> 00:37:19,598
He really seemed like a nice guy.

469
00:37:19,598 --> 00:37:21,870
Ah, yeah. Right.

470
00:37:26,701 --> 00:37:28,243
- Hey, so...
- Hey, so...

471
00:37:28,936 --> 00:37:29,811
You go first.

472
00:37:29,811 --> 00:37:31,346
You say it first.

473
00:37:33,415 --> 00:37:35,550
Actually, I'll go first.

474
00:37:37,352 --> 00:37:40,355
Do you want to have dinner
with Ja Yeong sometime?

475
00:37:44,989 --> 00:37:46,828
Is it too sudden?

476
00:37:47,929 --> 00:37:50,298
I don't mean to pressure you. It's just...

477
00:37:51,068 --> 00:37:52,500
I'd love to.

478
00:37:55,437 --> 00:37:57,172
Let's have dinner.

479
00:37:58,440 --> 00:37:59,841
Are you sure?

480
00:38:02,880 --> 00:38:04,548
- Go in.
- Yes.

481
00:38:04,548 --> 00:38:05,645
Hey.

482
00:38:05,645 --> 00:38:06,867
Yeah?

483
00:38:07,985 --> 00:38:09,686
Never mind. Go in.

484
00:38:09,686 --> 00:38:11,153
- Dad...
- Go in.

485
00:38:11,153 --> 00:38:14,355
- Ah, yes... Get home safe.
- Okay.

486
00:38:27,998 --> 00:38:31,067
Here is a story from listener "Midnight."

487
00:38:31,067 --> 00:38:35,010
Back when I worked the dawn shift
at a convenience store,

488
00:38:35,010 --> 00:38:37,267
there was a customer

489
00:38:37,267 --> 00:38:39,214
who always came in at the same time,

490
00:38:39,214 --> 00:38:42,801
wearing the same clothes to buy the same beer.

491
00:38:42,801 --> 00:38:44,085
What?

492
00:38:44,592 --> 00:38:46,634
She never spoke,

493
00:38:46,634 --> 00:38:49,123
and never showed any emotion.

494
00:38:50,167 --> 00:38:51,653
Seeing her

495
00:38:51,653 --> 00:38:55,496
felt like looking at myself.

496
00:38:59,835 --> 00:39:02,904
I think dawn is like that.

497
00:39:03,738 --> 00:39:06,074
A time when you can't hide anything.

498
00:39:07,196 --> 00:39:11,660
During the day, we pretend
to be happy or pretend not to be lonely.

499
00:39:11,660 --> 00:39:15,016
We can hide somewhere in between

500
00:39:15,016 --> 00:39:18,922
whether we are happy or lonely.

501
00:39:21,389 --> 00:39:23,625
But you can't do that at dawn.

502
00:39:25,593 --> 00:39:29,497
It's the time that lets you know for sure

503
00:39:30,866 --> 00:39:33,835
that you aren't in that middle ground.

504
00:39:36,972 --> 00:39:39,774
- She didn't ask anything...
- She didn't ask anything...

505
00:39:40,642 --> 00:39:43,011
- and didn't say anything.
- and didn't say anything.

506
00:39:45,033 --> 00:39:47,315
It was just comforting.

507
00:39:49,893 --> 00:39:52,387
Because she stayed with me...

508
00:39:53,634 --> 00:39:57,292
Because she was like me,
I wanted to say thank you,

509
00:39:58,963 --> 00:40:00,597
but I couldn't.

510
00:40:02,097 --> 00:40:05,833
She didn't come to buy beer
at that time anymore.

511
00:40:10,645 --> 00:40:12,974
I thought it was a relief.

512
00:40:14,311 --> 00:40:17,378
It seemed like she wasn't lonely anymore.

513
00:40:18,931 --> 00:40:20,615
Thank you.

514
00:40:22,090 --> 00:40:24,719
If we happen to meet next time,

515
00:40:25,234 --> 00:40:28,089
I'll buy you a beer.

516
00:41:07,634 --> 00:41:10,965
Didn't you say you didn't need any of it?

517
00:41:12,000 --> 00:41:13,034
Yes.

518
00:41:13,034 --> 00:41:14,501
I did say that.

519
00:41:14,501 --> 00:41:17,739
That was barely a week ago. Just a week.

520
00:41:17,739 --> 00:41:19,941
Did you suddenly need it all again?

521
00:41:21,498 --> 00:41:24,245
I thought I didn't need any of it,

522
00:41:24,934 --> 00:41:27,281
but I realized something important remained.

523
00:41:29,784 --> 00:41:33,688
Somehow, I thought you were too sentimental
for a STEM major.

524
00:41:36,024 --> 00:41:37,125
I'm sorry.

525
00:41:37,125 --> 00:41:40,397
Isn't it embarrassing to go back on your word

526
00:41:40,397 --> 00:41:42,397
like this?

527
00:41:44,103 --> 00:41:45,567
It is embarrassing.

528
00:41:45,567 --> 00:41:46,907
Gosh.

529
00:41:48,033 --> 00:41:50,671
Should I consider this effort?

530
00:41:51,339 --> 00:41:55,343
It's so hard to be fair.

531
00:41:56,011 --> 00:41:57,200
Hey.

532
00:41:57,200 --> 00:41:58,564
Did Professor Park's blurb come in?

533
00:41:58,564 --> 00:42:01,082
- Yes. I sent it to the printers a moment ago.
- Okay.

534
00:42:01,082 --> 00:42:02,283
- Marketing.
- Yes.

535
00:42:02,283 --> 00:42:03,744
Have you checked the interview schedule?

536
00:42:03,744 --> 00:42:04,694
Yes. Checking it right now.

537
00:42:04,694 --> 00:42:06,354
Let's speed things up.

538
00:42:06,354 --> 00:42:07,655
Sure.

539
00:42:08,556 --> 00:42:11,626
I decided to be an intern again.

540
00:42:12,403 --> 00:42:16,230
Thanks to you then, and thanks to you now.

541
00:42:38,934 --> 00:42:40,988
Where's the Ssamjang?

542
00:42:41,667 --> 00:42:43,124
Oh, here it is.

543
00:42:44,959 --> 00:42:47,295
Oh my, Raphael.

544
00:42:51,235 --> 00:42:52,700
Hello.

545
00:42:53,735 --> 00:42:55,300
Father.

546
00:42:55,300 --> 00:42:56,667
Fancy meeting you here.

547
00:42:56,667 --> 00:42:57,972
Right.

548
00:42:57,972 --> 00:43:01,634
We're taking Father to visit a new believer.

549
00:43:01,634 --> 00:43:02,246
Yes.

550
00:43:02,246 --> 00:43:04,345
How have you been doing lately?

551
00:43:05,248 --> 00:43:08,319
Thanks to your prayers, I'm doing well.

552
00:43:08,319 --> 00:43:11,019
You look so much better.

553
00:43:11,019 --> 00:43:13,788
You must be much more at peace now.

554
00:43:13,788 --> 00:43:15,325
Yes, thanks to you all.

555
00:43:16,257 --> 00:43:19,628
But they say that's not always the case.

556
00:43:19,628 --> 00:43:23,431
They say the first year after bereavement
is the most dangerous time.

557
00:43:23,431 --> 00:43:24,833
Let's finish shopping.

558
00:43:24,833 --> 00:43:28,402
I'm just so worried.

559
00:43:30,107 --> 00:43:31,496
Father.

560
00:43:31,496 --> 00:43:33,755
- We should visit Raphael's house too...
- Jin Ho.

561
00:43:33,755 --> 00:43:35,543
Is this enough?

562
00:43:37,479 --> 00:43:39,113
Who is she?

563
00:43:45,690 --> 00:43:47,321
Well...

564
00:43:48,092 --> 00:43:50,024
This is my girlfriend.

565
00:43:50,801 --> 00:43:52,521
Ja Yeong, please say hello.

566
00:43:52,521 --> 00:43:54,229
This is the Father from my church,

567
00:43:54,229 --> 00:43:56,164
the lady I mentioned,

568
00:43:56,164 --> 00:43:57,901
and other fellow members.

569
00:43:57,901 --> 00:43:59,370
Please say hello.

570
00:43:59,370 --> 00:44:00,435
Hello.

571
00:44:00,435 --> 00:44:02,203
Hello.

572
00:44:06,207 --> 00:44:08,581
Well, we need to finish shopping.

573
00:44:08,581 --> 00:44:10,077
Yes, go ahead.

574
00:44:14,351 --> 00:44:16,350
Honey, shall we go over there?

575
00:44:27,234 --> 00:44:28,619
Oh! Sorry.

576
00:44:28,619 --> 00:44:30,000
It's okay.

577
00:44:30,000 --> 00:44:32,458
One, two, three, four.

578
00:44:32,458 --> 00:44:34,001
I need to get more out.

579
00:44:34,698 --> 00:44:35,859
Smells good.

580
00:44:35,859 --> 00:44:37,078
Could you taste this?

581
00:44:37,078 --> 00:44:38,358
Sure.

582
00:44:38,358 --> 00:44:39,786
Be careful, it's hot.

583
00:44:41,601 --> 00:44:43,234
Wait.

584
00:44:43,234 --> 00:44:45,980
Oh, someone must be here already.

585
00:44:52,799 --> 00:44:54,288
You're earlier than I expected.

586
00:44:55,039 --> 00:44:56,705
Yes.

587
00:44:56,705 --> 00:44:58,292
Hello.

588
00:44:58,863 --> 00:45:00,634
Hello.

589
00:45:00,634 --> 00:45:01,999
Well...

590
00:45:01,999 --> 00:45:03,564
This is...

591
00:45:06,300 --> 00:45:08,072
Uh, hey...

592
00:45:08,072 --> 00:45:11,406
Could you taste this soup for me?

593
00:45:11,406 --> 00:45:12,843
Sure.

594
00:45:19,049 --> 00:45:20,868
How is it?

595
00:45:20,868 --> 00:45:22,482
I think

596
00:45:22,482 --> 00:45:24,889
it's a little bland.

597
00:45:24,889 --> 00:45:26,387
Really?

598
00:45:28,389 --> 00:45:29,557
I think it's fine.

599
00:45:29,557 --> 00:45:31,125
Oh, really?

600
00:45:34,932 --> 00:45:36,164
Is it?

601
00:45:36,164 --> 00:45:37,699
Is it bland?

602
00:45:37,699 --> 00:45:39,467
I'm not sure.

603
00:45:41,205 --> 00:45:42,667
- What's wrong?
- What's wrong?

604
00:45:43,968 --> 00:45:45,239
No,

605
00:45:46,040 --> 00:45:48,509
the seasoning seems fine.

606
00:45:48,509 --> 00:45:51,512
Why are you two acting so natural?

607
00:45:54,996 --> 00:45:57,986
- Should I let it boil a bit more then?
- No.

608
00:45:57,986 --> 00:46:01,789
It might get too salty. I think it's fine now.

609
00:46:12,900 --> 00:46:14,114
Are you doing okay?

610
00:46:14,114 --> 00:46:17,338
The fire just won't start.

611
00:46:17,338 --> 00:46:19,173
Oh? I haven't seen this before.
Did we always have this?

612
00:46:19,173 --> 00:46:21,075
I bought a new one.

613
00:46:21,075 --> 00:46:22,644
I wondered if I'd actually use it much.

614
00:46:22,644 --> 00:46:25,012
But I thought having it would make me use it.

615
00:46:26,848 --> 00:46:28,683
That was a good idea.

616
00:46:35,456 --> 00:46:37,132
I'm home.

617
00:46:37,132 --> 00:46:39,026
- Hi.
- You're home.

618
00:46:41,329 --> 00:46:43,066
Hi, Bom.

619
00:46:45,133 --> 00:46:47,661
You remember me, right?

620
00:46:48,138 --> 00:46:49,804
Have you been doing well?

621
00:46:55,910 --> 00:46:57,335
Hello.

622
00:46:57,335 --> 00:46:58,646
Ah, yeah.

623
00:46:58,646 --> 00:47:00,314
Hello.

624
00:47:00,882 --> 00:47:03,395
He's handsome, unlike you.

625
00:47:03,395 --> 00:47:04,388
What?

626
00:47:04,388 --> 00:47:07,495
I'm not bad-looking myself.

627
00:47:07,495 --> 00:47:11,058
Look. Smoke follows handsome people.

628
00:47:13,261 --> 00:47:15,296
I'll get it.

629
00:47:16,196 --> 00:47:17,732
Yeah.

630
00:47:20,671 --> 00:47:21,939
Yeah.

631
00:47:21,939 --> 00:47:23,337
Jun Seo.

632
00:47:24,072 --> 00:47:26,179
- Long time no see.
- Yeah.

633
00:47:26,179 --> 00:47:27,808
It has been a while.

634
00:47:29,711 --> 00:47:31,879
- Please come in.
- Yes.

635
00:47:36,387 --> 00:47:38,999
Come on in. You have to say hello.

636
00:47:38,999 --> 00:47:40,324
Welcome.

637
00:47:40,324 --> 00:47:41,923
Hello.

638
00:47:41,923 --> 00:47:43,279
Hello.

639
00:47:43,279 --> 00:47:45,893
You must be Daniel.

640
00:47:45,893 --> 00:47:48,562
You're handsome, just like your dad.

641
00:47:49,099 --> 00:47:52,067
- Here... this is for you.
- Oh, you shouldn't have.

642
00:47:52,067 --> 00:47:54,101
Come this way, please.

643
00:47:55,169 --> 00:47:57,004
Hello.

644
00:47:58,773 --> 00:48:00,686
This is for me?

645
00:48:00,686 --> 00:48:02,810
It's so pretty.

646
00:48:07,051 --> 00:48:09,201
Okay, please take a seat.

647
00:48:13,821 --> 00:48:16,157
- Thank you for the food.
- Enjoy it.

648
00:48:16,157 --> 00:48:18,926
He still doesn't know how to make a ssam.

649
00:48:18,926 --> 00:48:22,897
You need to add garlic and peppers
when you eat meat.

650
00:48:22,897 --> 00:48:24,031
- Here.
- Oh, come on.

651
00:48:24,031 --> 00:48:25,994
- Dad.
- Just add one more.

652
00:48:25,994 --> 00:48:26,837
Oh, Dad.

653
00:48:26,837 --> 00:48:30,304
It's spicy so it cuts the grease.
It's good. Try it.

654
00:48:31,906 --> 00:48:33,143
How is it? Good, right?

655
00:48:33,143 --> 00:48:34,809
Oh, don't eat it. Gosh.

656
00:48:34,809 --> 00:48:35,513
What's wrong?

657
00:48:35,513 --> 00:48:37,712
- It's too spicy.
- Oh my goodness.

658
00:48:37,712 --> 00:48:39,980
- Water, please.
- Dad!

659
00:48:52,493 --> 00:48:58,098
[Tonight, he weighs heavily on her heart]

660
00:49:02,634 --> 00:49:04,375
Hey.

661
00:49:04,375 --> 00:49:06,641
Oh, seriously.

662
00:49:06,641 --> 00:49:09,677
Dad, he can't handle spicy food.

663
00:49:09,677 --> 00:49:11,112
No, definitely not.

664
00:49:11,112 --> 00:49:12,616
Are you okay?

665
00:49:12,616 --> 00:49:15,048
Just swallow it. Swallow it.

666
00:49:15,750 --> 00:49:16,767
Do you want to spit it out?

667
00:49:16,767 --> 00:49:18,853
Look how red his face is.

668
00:49:18,853 --> 00:49:21,225
- I'm going out for a bit.
- Okay.

669
00:49:21,225 --> 00:49:22,868
Let's toast with water.

670
00:49:22,868 --> 00:49:24,491
Cheers.

671
00:50:39,934 --> 00:50:45,639
[Matna Pork Cutlet]

672
00:50:46,941 --> 00:50:49,680
Only pork cutlet? Isn't it dry?

673
00:50:49,680 --> 00:50:52,680
One jjolmyeon, please.

674
00:50:57,485 --> 00:50:59,473
What are you doing?

675
00:50:59,473 --> 00:51:01,588
It was a little painful,

676
00:51:03,367 --> 00:51:05,259
not seeing you for a few days

677
00:51:06,133 --> 00:51:07,594
and not being able

678
00:51:09,267 --> 00:51:10,864
to contact you.

679
00:51:12,500 --> 00:51:14,501
I didn't realize it before,

680
00:51:16,934 --> 00:51:18,439
but actually, I...

681
00:51:22,743 --> 00:51:25,467
I think I like cutting pork cutlets for you.

682
00:51:25,467 --> 00:51:27,017
Yeah.

683
00:51:27,017 --> 00:51:28,983
What are you talking about?

684
00:51:31,185 --> 00:51:34,521
I like stealing the cutlet I cut for you.

685
00:51:36,791 --> 00:51:38,759
And I love

686
00:51:41,329 --> 00:51:44,131
the loud way you eat the pork cutlet

687
00:51:48,601 --> 00:51:50,137
that I sliced for you.

688
00:51:52,701 --> 00:51:54,274
So...

689
00:52:02,334 --> 00:52:03,454
So what?

690
00:52:03,454 --> 00:52:05,167
So, this is on me.

691
00:52:05,167 --> 00:52:06,720
Gosh.

692
00:52:07,291 --> 00:52:09,193
Just this?

693
00:52:09,193 --> 00:52:11,000
Hey.

694
00:52:11,000 --> 00:52:12,726
I'm still a student.

695
00:52:19,336 --> 00:52:20,901
Eat this.

696
00:52:21,739 --> 00:52:23,003
Say, "Ah."

697
00:52:35,801 --> 00:52:36,954
Is it good?

698
00:52:36,954 --> 00:52:38,567
Yeah.

699
00:52:38,567 --> 00:52:39,292
Is it that good?

700
00:52:39,292 --> 00:52:41,934
The summer that was unusually loud

701
00:52:41,934 --> 00:52:43,957
and hot

702
00:52:45,162 --> 00:52:47,761
was coming to an end like this.

703
00:52:49,892 --> 00:52:52,266
And just like that, the seasons passed.

704
00:52:53,234 --> 00:52:55,302
And other seasons

705
00:52:56,207 --> 00:52:57,844
arrived.

706
00:52:59,006 --> 00:52:59,940
[Driving test vehicle]

707
00:52:59,940 --> 00:53:01,874
Some seasons taught me

708
00:53:01,874 --> 00:53:04,617
that things I feared

709
00:53:05,380 --> 00:53:08,133
weren't actually that big of a deal.

710
00:53:08,133 --> 00:53:11,018
Vehicle No. 15, you passed.

711
00:53:13,334 --> 00:53:15,789
Seasons that gave us the joy

712
00:53:17,124 --> 00:53:20,294
of growing to resemble each other
in our clumsiness.

713
00:53:23,567 --> 00:53:26,038
Seasons that marked the end

714
00:53:26,038 --> 00:53:28,136
of long-held plans and preparations.

715
00:53:28,136 --> 00:53:29,203
[Congrats on resigning, future great writer!]
Ta-da!

716
00:53:29,203 --> 00:53:31,238
Congrats on resigning!

717
00:53:33,174 --> 00:53:35,909
No matter how much we anticipated and prepared,

718
00:53:37,343 --> 00:53:39,780
there were seasons

719
00:53:40,534 --> 00:53:42,717
where sadness was unavoidable.

720
00:53:42,717 --> 00:53:45,119
Thank you for coming to me as my daughter.

721
00:53:45,601 --> 00:53:47,955
Thank you

722
00:53:48,601 --> 00:53:50,424
for making me a mom.

723
00:53:50,424 --> 00:53:52,506
Through all the bitter,

724
00:53:53,601 --> 00:53:55,295
healing,

725
00:53:56,500 --> 00:53:58,365
warm,

726
00:53:59,701 --> 00:54:01,401
fluttering,

727
00:54:04,405 --> 00:54:07,141
and cold moments...

728
00:54:09,000 --> 00:54:10,577
several seasons

729
00:54:11,902 --> 00:54:14,348
have stacked up behind us,

730
00:54:17,801 --> 00:54:19,212
and now,

731
00:54:20,567 --> 00:54:22,289
a new spring

732
00:54:23,601 --> 00:54:25,126
is blooming.

733
00:54:25,126 --> 00:54:27,494
[Welcome, new students of Seongeun University!]

734
00:54:41,145 --> 00:54:43,143
Five minutes left.

735
00:54:47,618 --> 00:54:50,618
Holding onto it now means there's no hope.

736
00:54:50,618 --> 00:54:52,586
Just a few more seconds, please!

737
00:54:53,123 --> 00:54:54,306
Sure.

738
00:54:54,306 --> 00:54:55,856
Even those five minutes

739
00:54:55,856 --> 00:54:58,367
are part of your hard-earned tuition.

740
00:54:58,367 --> 00:55:00,027
Use it all.

741
00:55:02,199 --> 00:55:04,865
Hello, TA.

742
00:55:05,706 --> 00:55:07,734
Long time no see.

743
00:55:08,281 --> 00:55:10,542
Yeah, it really has been a while.

744
00:55:10,542 --> 00:55:12,639
- Hello, Professor.
- Hello.

745
00:55:14,041 --> 00:55:15,342
I'm so jealous.

746
00:55:15,342 --> 00:55:16,422
Look at you, Professor.

747
00:55:16,422 --> 00:55:18,961
Stick close to Professor Song too.

748
00:55:18,961 --> 00:55:20,147
You never know.

749
00:55:20,147 --> 00:55:22,182
Come on... me?

750
00:55:23,261 --> 00:55:25,841
Since you're done, let's grab a meal.

751
00:55:25,841 --> 00:55:29,390
I have a class,
so I have to head to Ansan. Sorry.

752
00:55:29,390 --> 00:55:31,491
Oh, okay.

753
00:55:32,329 --> 00:55:33,927
Bye.

754
00:56:05,868 --> 00:56:08,265
I'm being so pathetic, aren't I?

755
00:56:08,265 --> 00:56:10,267
Just awful.

756
00:56:10,267 --> 00:56:11,665
Well...

757
00:56:13,000 --> 00:56:15,969
You're acting sentimental,
unlike your usual self.

758
00:56:16,901 --> 00:56:18,505
It's actually kind of sexy.

759
00:56:26,046 --> 00:56:29,086
You dated for so long,
and finally, it's happening.

760
00:56:29,086 --> 00:56:31,315
Of course. Too much time invested
in breaking up.

761
00:56:31,315 --> 00:56:34,042
Everyone uses mobile invites these days.

762
00:56:34,042 --> 00:56:35,801
They insisted on doing every little thing
for the wedding.

763
00:56:35,801 --> 00:56:37,024
I heard they almost broke up over it.

764
00:56:37,024 --> 00:56:39,163
I'm not giving you the bouquet.

765
00:56:39,163 --> 00:56:41,362
I'm heading out first.

766
00:56:41,362 --> 00:56:43,915
You didn't forget next Saturday, right?

767
00:56:43,915 --> 00:56:45,799
Right, I won't forget.

768
00:56:45,799 --> 00:56:47,134
- I'm heading off now.
- Have a good one.

769
00:56:47,134 --> 00:56:48,969
Bye.

770
00:56:49,807 --> 00:56:51,805
I think I'm gonna be late.

771
00:56:51,805 --> 00:56:53,307
Traffic is bad.

772
00:56:53,307 --> 00:56:55,412
What about the flowers? Did you get them?

773
00:56:55,885 --> 00:56:57,106
Shoot! What should I do?

774
00:56:57,106 --> 00:56:58,801
It'll take too long to find a florist.

775
00:56:58,801 --> 00:57:00,084
Then...

776
00:57:00,084 --> 00:57:02,616
I'll buy them! Just get there quickly.

777
00:57:02,616 --> 00:57:03,886
Drive safely,

778
00:57:03,886 --> 00:57:05,919
but hurry up!

779
00:57:28,242 --> 00:57:30,944
[Daniel, you're the best!]

780
00:57:58,634 --> 00:58:00,578
Everyone else is already out here...

781
00:58:00,578 --> 00:58:01,734
Isn't it that way?

782
00:58:01,734 --> 00:58:03,905
- Dad.
- Yeah.

783
00:58:03,905 --> 00:58:06,124
Congrats! You were amazing.

784
00:58:06,124 --> 00:58:08,382
I thought you were going to smash the drums.

785
00:58:08,382 --> 00:58:10,087
Total

786
00:58:10,087 --> 00:58:11,400
Aerosmith vibes.

787
00:58:11,400 --> 00:58:12,486
No.

788
00:58:12,486 --> 00:58:14,788
I wasn't that good.

789
00:58:14,788 --> 00:58:16,004
He's sweating quite a lot.

790
00:58:16,004 --> 00:58:17,557
Daniel.

791
00:58:19,296 --> 00:58:20,894
Mom!

792
00:58:24,201 --> 00:58:25,828
When did you get here?

793
00:58:25,828 --> 00:58:27,601
I got here yesterday.

794
00:58:34,912 --> 00:58:36,676
Long time no see.

795
00:58:38,449 --> 00:58:39,892
Yeah.

796
00:58:43,434 --> 00:58:45,118
Hello.

797
00:58:47,358 --> 00:58:50,027
Oh... Hello.

798
00:58:50,027 --> 00:58:52,359
I've heard a lot about you.
